- If user clicks play while quit rebuild in progress, _busy true blocks. Button not disabled but okay. Could disable play during busy via `setBusyUI` optional. Not critical but UX. Add `this.playBtn.disabled = busy` maybe style. We can set.
- After startGame, `_busy=false` in finally. During build the loading overlay blocks clicks.

`showLoading` on startGame when rebuilding only. If seed same reuse, no loading. Good. At boot loading visible.

`enterGame` calls `this.showLoading(false)` to ensure hidden.

`buildSession` at start calls `this.showLoading(true)` maybe always. During quit we already show. Fine.
`buildSession` sets `this.state='loading'`, then after returns `state` remains 'loading' until caller sets. In init sets menu; startGame sets playing; quit sets menu.
If called from startGame, `showLoading(true)`; after build setLoading 1 then `enterGame` hides. Good.

`disposeSession` must not null `this.hud`, `this.input`, `this.camera`. It nulls session-specific.

`this.scene` old -> after dispose new Scene. Renderer render called during build with old scene? The loop doesn't run yet at boot. During quit rebuild, loop is running; `this.scene` is still old scene while disposing; then set new. tick state 'loading' has no branch. Loop will render `this.scene` if exists; if old was set null maybe skip. Add tick loading: just render. After dispose sets scene null, renderer clears? If `this.scene` null, `renderer.clear()`. Good. Then new scene blank black with loading overlay. Fine.

